# FORM trace caches created by the gen_*_form.wls timing scripts (regenerable; the scripts
# empty their own cache at startup so each run is a clean cold trace).
TraceCache_*form/
# stray TensorBases cache if a script runs with cwd=numtracer (the canonical one is at repo root)
TBCache/

# compile_bench.sh run artifacts (the script + bench/iso TUs are the deliverable, not the outputs)
bench/compile_bench.*.txt
bench/compile_bench.*.report
bench/compile_bench.*.report.json

# Numeric-backend GENERATOR intermediates: the MakeNTKernel "Numeric" path emits a build-time
# generator program (main TU + per-net unit TUs + a decl header) into tests/gen/, compiles+runs it
# to produce the committed straight-line kernels, then the program is disposable. Only the FINAL
# kernels (*_kernel.hh / *_kernels.hh) are the deliverable; these regenerable intermediates were
# ~62 MB of repo bloat. The gen_*.wls SOURCE scripts (different extension) are kept.
tests/gen/gen_*.cpp
tests/gen/gen_*_nets.hh
# ...and the per-flow precompiled-header source the unit TUs compile against (see NT_GEN_PCH).
tests/gen/gen_*_pch.hh
# The lambda3d fixtures DELIBERATELY track their emitted generator sources (they are the fixture, see
# tests/gen/lambda3d/), so the blanket gen_*.cpp / gen_*_nets.hh rules above must not be extended to
# the subdirectories. The precompiled header is different: it is a pure build artifact with no
# fixture value, and it is regenerated on every run — so ignore it there too.
tests/gen/*/gen_*_pch.hh

# CMake writes NumTracerPaths.m (from cmake/NumTracerPaths.m.in) into the BUILD dir and installs it
# beside NumTracer.m, recording where the C++ headers landed. A copy was also committed here, which
# is worse than useless: it carried one machine's absolute install path, and Codegen.m's
# resolveIncludeDir reads $NumTracerDirectory/NumTracerPaths.m — so in a source-tree run the STALE
# committed copy is what won. It is generated; it is not source.
mathematica/NumTracerPaths.m
